ner_results: This is a shared visit for services provided by me, ***** ***** *****, MD. I performed a face-to-face encounter with the patient and the following portion of the note is my own. Today the patient still appears more confused and less of herself. She missed the scheduled <1>MRI</1> from last Friday and we will reschedule. She has denied all <2>drug use</2> or excessive <3>pain medications</3>. Her <4>electrolytes</4> and other <5>labs</5> do not offer any reason for her confusion. Await the repeat <6>MRI</6>. Continue current therapy until clear evidence of progression. SUBJECTIVE ***** ***** is a 44 y.o. female with ***** <7>Syndrome</7> and early stage <8>endometrial cancer</8> and <9>colon cancer</9> and now with newly diagnosed <10>metastatic breast cancer</10> who started <11>irinotecan</11> on <12>06/30/19</12>. Due to <13>transaminitis</13> and <14>diarrhea</14> her treatment has been missed her day 8 treatments with every cycle so far. She presents today for <15>cycle 3 day 1</15>. She came last Thursday to get <16>chemotherapy</16> since she had missed her chemotherapy the week prior but she was not scheduled for it, so she was sent home. She had an appointment with Dr. ***** in ***** ***** to discuss <17>XRT to S1</17> but did not go to the appointment. On <18>Cycle 2 day 4</18> she called in reports <19>watery diarrhea</19> with <20>fecal incontinence</20> which resolved with <21>imodium</21>. <22>Urination</22> normal. She had mild <23>nausea</23> after treatment for which she did not take any <24>antiemetics</24>. Her nausea continues, first thing in the morning. Occasionally <25>vomits</25>. Then takes <26>compazine</26> with relief. <27>Weight</27> stable. Now having a <28>protein shakes</28> in the AM. She has been feeling really <29>tired</29> the last few days. Wants to sleep right now. Her <30>chest pain</30> is back again, not as bad as before. Looks like it's a little red again as well. Had a <31>fever</31> of <32>103</32> but able to reduce it with ***** and a <33>cold towel</33>. But then it came up again twice later that day but she had ***** a ***** of blankets on herself. So since that day she has stopped. 
