4. <1>Lytic S1 vertebral body lesion</1>: maximum <2>SUV</2> of 6.6. <3>Lymph nodes</3>: Index nodes as described above. Additional <4>hypermetabolic right internal mammary node</4> is 0.6 x 0.8 cm (series 4 1 image 75 with a maximum <5>SUV</5> of 4.3. The <6>hypermetabolic caudate lobe lesion</6> is markedly increased in size when compared to prior <7>CT abdomen/pelvis</7> from 09/29/2018. Additional <8>hypoattenuating, hypermetabolic segment VII lesion</8> is 1.3 x 1.7 x 1.5 cm with a maximum <9>SUV</9> of 11.2 02/25/19 <10>Liver biopsy</10>: <11>triple negative metastatic breast cancer</11> *****/*****/***** - *****/*****/***** <12>Abraxane</12> and <13>Pembrolizumab</13> 05/31/19 <14>PET/CT</14>: significantly increased number and extent of <15>hypermetabolic metastases</15> including <16>osseous lesions</16>, <17>hepatic lesions</17>, <18>nodal lesions</18>, and <19>chest wall lesions</19>. New linear hypermetabolism extending along the central and left aspect of <20>clivus</20> and <21>petrous bone</21> with suggestion of possible underlying osseous irregularity, concerning for <22>intracranial and/or skull base involvement</22> but incompletely evaluated on this exam. New <23>hypermetabolic lesions in bilateral femoral necks</23>, which may place patient at risk for <24>pathologic fracture</24>. *****/*****/***** - *****/*****/***** admitted to ***** with <25>fever</25>, <26>chest pain/swelling</26>, and <27>low back pain</27>. Found to have <28>chest wall cellulitis</28> and given <29>ABX</29>. Imaging done - see below. 06/11/19 <30>MRI lumbar spine</30>: Numerous <31>bone marrow replacing lesion in the lumbar spine and in the pelvis</31>, most pronounced at <32>S1 with endplate fracture</32>. 06/13/19 <33>CT CAP</33>: Interval development of <34>subcutaneous edema in the ventral chest wall soft tissues</34>, without drainable fluid collection, suspicious for <35>soft tissue infection/cellulitis</35>. Slightly more hypodense appearance of enhancing nodules in the <36>right chest wall</36> and <37>right pectoralis musculature</37>. Unchanged adjacent <38>right internal mammary lymphadenopathy</38>. New <39>trace pleural effusions</39> with increase in <40>pericardial recess</40>.
``` 
