HPI:  ***** ***** is a 34 y.o. female with <1>ER+/PR+ IDC</1> of the <2>right breast</2>. On June 21 she underwent a <3>partial mastectomy</3> with <4>sentinel node biopsy</4> with <5>expander placement</5>. She reports recovering well although is still experiencing tightness in the area. Experiences <6>night sweats</6> for four days after <7>injection</7>. Otherwise manageable. Patient Active Problem List Diagnosis Date Noted  <8>Breast Cancer Right</8> 04/25/2019 December 2018 self-palpated <9>right breast mass</9> 03/05/2019 <10>Bilateral breast US</10> (***** ***** Hospital in *****): <11>6x7 mm mass</11> with <12>ductal extension</12> at 1 o'clock, likely <13>DCIS</13>. 03/17/2019 <14>Gynecology</14> at ***** for <15>lower abdomen swelling</15>, <16>urethral discomfort</16> and <17>breast mass</17> in the <18>breast US</18> (*****). On exam <19>1 cm firm, mobile, nontender mass</19> approximately <20>5 cm from nipple</20> at 1 o'clock. 03/17/2019: <21>Right breast FNA</21> at 1 o'clock (UCSF): <22>Benign</22> and could be seen in the setting of <23>fibrocystic change</23> or <24>fibroadenoma</24>. 03/17/2018 <25>Abdomen-pelvic CT</25>: <26>No acute findings</26> (for <27>abdominal pain</27>). 03/28/2019 <28>Bilateral breast diagnostic mammogram</28> (UCSF): A <29>focal asymmetry</29> is suggested in the region. <30>Triangular marker</30> denotes site of <31>focal pain</31> in the <32>lower slightly outer right breast</32>, with <33>no underlying mammographic correlate</33>. <34>Scattered and occasionally grouped benign-appearing microcalcifications</34>, <35>both breasts</35>, predominantly <36>coarse dystrophic</36>, likely the sequelae of reported <37>fat grafting</37>. 03/28/2019 <38>Bilateral breast diagnostic US</38>(UCSF): <39>22 x 10 x 15 mm oval complex solid and cystic mass</39> with <40>peripheral echogenicity</40> and an <41>irregular, antiparallel hypoechoic central component</41> in the <42>right upper inner quadrant</42>, 1:00, <43>8 cm from nipple</43>. The <44>central hypoechoic component</44> measures up to <45>10 mm</45>. <46>No sonographic correlate</46> to site of <47>focal pain</47> in the <48>lower outer right breast</48> at 7 o'clock, <49>5 cm from nipple</49>. <50>No sonographic correlate</50> to clinician's site of concern in the <51>left axilla</51>. A few <52>normal-appearing nodes</52> are identified.
