ner_results: ```plaintext
There is no edema in the adjacent brain parenchyma. <1>Ureteral based metastases</1> are present along the <2>posterior interhemispheric falx</2> and <3>parasagittal convexity</3> bilaterally. There is no edema in the adjacent brain parenchyma. Additionally, small punctate foci of <4>contrast enhancement</4> are noted in the <5>right cerebellar hemisphere</5> inferiorly and posteriorly. It is not clear whether these are small <6>parenchymal metastases</6> or <7>meningeal tumor</7>. There is an approximately <8>15 mm metastases</8> in the <9>upper clivus</9> (skull). <10>02/10/17: BRCA1/2 negative</10>. <11>02/11/17 CT A/P w/ contrast</11>: <12>Right breast skin thickening</12> is partially imaged. <13>Minimal bibasilar atelectasis</13>. <14>Right lower lobe posterior medial soft tissue thickening</14> along the <15>pleural surface</15>. Few small <16>right cardiophrenic angle lymph nodes</16> are more numerous than normally seen. <17>Small retroperitoneal lymph nodes</17> are predominantly under 1 cm. <18>Extensive bony lytic destructive appearance</18> to the <19>left inferior pubic ramus</19> with <20>subacute/healing fractures</20> suggested. <21>Old right inferior pubic ramus fracture</21> is also seen as well as <22>lytic appearance of the left greater than right acetabulum</22>. <23>Small nondisplaced fracture of the left sacral ala</23> likely pathologic with <24>diffuse osseous metastatic involvement</24> of the <25>sacrum</25> and <26>iliac bones</26> as well as throughout the <27>lumbar vertebral bodies</27> and in <28>multiple ribs</28>. <29>Several healing left and right rib fractures</29> are seen also likely pathologic. <30>Mild degenerative disc disease L4-5</30>. <31>Several endplate compression fracture deformities</31>, for example, <32>inferior endplate compression of T12</32>. <33>Large lytic lesion</33> destroys and replaces much of <34>T10</34>. <35>02/11/17 bilateral diagnostic mammogram</35> and <36>limited right breast US</36>: The <37>breast tissue</37> is fatty with scattered <38>fibroglandular elements</38>. In the <39>right breast</39> at <40>12 o'clock middle third</40>, there is a <41>large spiculated mass</41> containing <42>numerous suspicious calcifications</42>. There is <43>diffuse overlying skin thickening</43> as well. No suspicious findings.
``` 
