noted LABS: IMAGING/PATHOLOGY: As noted above in ***** ASSESSMENT/PLAN: *****-***** ***** is a 41 y.o. female with recently diagnosed left nuclear grade 2 <1>ER+</1> <2>DCIS</2> s/p left partial <3>mastectomy</3> here to discuss systemic therapy options. We discussed that <4>DCIS</4> is a surgical disease. The primary treatment is definitive surgery which she has had. I encouraged to meet with <5>radiation oncology</5> to discuss adjuvant <6>radiation</6> and its benefit in reducing local/regional recurrence. I explained that <7>DCIS</7> can return 50% of the time as another insitu disease and 50% of the time as invasive disease, but technically it should not result in distant recurrence due to lack of invasion. We discussed the role of systemic therapy with <8>tamoxifen</8>. We reviewed the ***** <9>B-24 study</9> that did show a statistically significant reduction in recurrence risk with 5 years of *****, albeit the benefit was small and the side effects are not insignificant. In particular the reduction in invasive disease was 3% with <10>tamoxifen</10>, the remaining benefit in non-invasive disease. No difference in distant recurrence or survival. We discussed the potential side effects including but not limited to <11>hot flashes</11>, <12>vaginal discharge</12>, <13>headache/migraines</13>, <14>vaginal dryness</14>, <15>mood instability</15>, <16>sexual dysfunction</16>, <17>ovarian cysts</17>, increase in <18>fibroids</18>, impact on uterus including ***** and <19>abnormal vaginal bleeding</19>, as well as small increase risk of <20>endometrial cancer</20> (0.5%) and <21>thrombosis</21> (1-2%). We discussed that she is unable to get pregnant on <22>tamoxifen</22>. The patient will think about the risk/benefit. I reassured her that her prognosis is excellent. We discussed other lifestyle factors to consider including exercise, healthy <23>BMI</23> <30, reducing <24>etoh</24>. 1. The patient concerns were discussed in detail. Patient verbalizes understanding of these issues and agrees with the plan. 2. Reviewed treatment options, treatment side effects in detail. 3. I reviewed the patient's medical information and medical history. 4. I have reviewed the past medical, family, and social history sections including the medications and allergies listed in the above medical record. 5. Total face to face time: 60 min Total counseling time: 50 min
