ner_results: ```plaintext
dissection. Pathology from the <1>left breast</1> revealed no <2>cancer</2>, and 0/8 <3>axillary lymph nodes</3> contained metastatic <4>cancer</4>. However in the <5>right breast mastectomy specimen</5>, there was was 2 cm of <6>grade 1 invasive ductal cancer</6>. 0 of 6 <7>lymph nodes</7> removed contained <8>cancer</8> on the right side. The <9>invasive cancer</9> was again <10>estrogen receptor positive</10>, <11>progesterone receptor negative</11>, and <12>HER-2/neu negative</12>. November 2009 the patient initiated <13>letrozole</13>. October 2010 the patient began to experience some <14>lightheadedness</14> when standing. She then developed more severe <15>headaches</15>. Finally she noted a <16>lump</16> in the <17>left side of her neck</17>. 12/06/2010 the patient underwent a <18>fine-needle aspiration</18> of a <19>left supraclavicular lymph node</19> which revealed <20>metastatic adenocarcinoma</20> which was very weakly <21>estrogen receptor positive</21> with only 1-5% of the cells staining, <22>progesterone receptor negative</22>, and <23>HER-2/neu negative</23>. 12/11/2010 the patient underwent a <24>PET CT scan</24> which revealed a new <25>right frontal dural based metastasis</25> with <26>SUV of 28.2</26> with surrounding <27>vasogenic edema</27> and <28>mass effect</28>. The scan also revealed multiple <29>hypermetabolic left cervical and supraclavicular lymph nodes</29> consistent with <30>metastatic disease</30>. There was <31>hypermetabolism</31> along the <32>right parasternal chest wall</32> consistent with <33>recurrent disease</33> possibly invading the <34>sternum</34>. There was also <35>bilateral subpectoral lymphadenopathy</35> with maximum <36>SUV of 11.4</36> on the left and <37>4.1</37> on the right. There was an area of <38>focal hypermetabolism</38> in the <39>hepatic segment</39> ***** ***** ***** ***** ***** ***** a maximum <40>SUV of 7.0</40> suspicious for early <41>hepatic metastasis</41>. There was <42>multifocal osseous metastatic disease</42> identified within the <43>C2</43>, <44>L2 vertebral bodies</44> as well as in the <45>sacrum</45>. 12/11/2010 the patient underwent an <46>MRI of the brain</46> which revealed a <47>4 cm left inferior frontal extra-axial mass</47> new since 11/08/2009. Patient met with <48>radiation oncology</48> as
``` 
