ner_results: ```plaintext
well as neurosurgery to discuss treatment options. 12/30/2010 the patient underwent <1>resection</1> of the <2>frontal brain metastasis</2>. Pathology confirmed that it was consistent with a <3>metastatic adenocarcinoma</3> of <4>breast primary</4>, and was <5>estrogen receptor negative</5>, <6>progesterone receptor negative</6>, and <7>HER-2/neu negative</7>. 02/10/2011 - <8>Whole brain RT</8>: <9>30 gray</9> in <10>10 fractions</10> 03/01/2011 - Started <11>Xeloda</11> <12>4000mg</12> (actually took <13>2000mg</13>) <14>daily</14> <15>14 days on 7 days off</15> 03/12/2011 - <16>PET/CT</16> (during cycle 1 <17>Xeloda</17>) with <18>PD</18> including <19>liver</19>, <20>bones</20>, <21>LNs</21>, <22>breast</22>. Exam with new <23>chest wall/breast skin metastases</23>. 03/19/2011 - Started <24>ixabepilone</24> <25>40mg/m2</25> *****, <26>Xeloda</26> continued, started <27>denosumab</27>
``` 
