 characterize are again noted. <1>Left renal cysts</1> are seen. The remainder of the abdomen and pelvis is unremarkable. No <2>hypermetabolic lymphadenopathy</2>. Musculoskeletal: Multiple <3>osseous lesions</3> involving the thoracolumbar and sternum are not changed in size since prior study and do not demonstrate hypermetabolic activity, consistent with treated <4>metastases</4>. <5>Left iliac wing sclerotic lesion</5> is unchanged in size and metabolic activity with an <6>SUV of 3.1</6>. Persistent <7>FDG uptake</7> within <8>left L1 pedicle</8> (<9>SUV 6</9>) and <10>anterior vertebral body</10> (<11>SUV 9</11>) is not significantly changed since prior. Interval decrease in activity of previously described <12>L2 vertebral body sclerotic focus</12> with no residual hypermetabolic activity seen. No new <13>osseous lesions</13> are identified. IMPRESSION: 1. Stable to slightly decreased metabolic activity of <14>osseous metastases</14>. No new <15>metastases</15> are identified. This study was reviewed by attendings Dr. ***** ***** from Abdominal Imaging and Dr. ***** ***** ***** of Nuclear Medicine. I have individually visualized and interpreted the above ***** ASSESSMENT & PLAN <16>Hormone positive MBC to bone</16> with stable disease. Continue on *****, <17>zoladex</17> and <18>femara</18>. Reassess <19>lower back pain</19> at two weeks and consider <20>MRI of the spine</20>. Patient to rtc if pain worsens. Possible <21>UTI</21> vs. <22>Genital-urinary symptoms from estrogen depletion</22>. Obtain <23>UA</23> Easy bruising per patient, obtain <24>CBC with platelets</24>. The patient concerns were discussed in detail. Patient verbalizes understanding of these issues and agrees with the plan. Reviewed treatment options, treatment side effects in detail. I reviewed the patient's medical information and medical history. I have reviewed the past medical, family, and social history sections including the medications and allergies listed in the above medical record. Electronically signed by: ***** *****, *****/*****/***** *****:***** PM
