Additional low-level <1>hypermetabolism</1> along the anterior <2>right breast tissue expander</2> is also favored to reflect <3>postprocedural changes</3>; correlate clinically for <4>superimposed infection</4>. Associated low-level <5>hypermetabolism</5> in <6>left greater than right axillary/subpectoral nodes</6> is nonspecific in the setting of <7>ongoing infection</7>. Incidental <8>right thyroid nodule</8> measuring up to 2.1 cm with associated <9>FDG uptake</9>. Recommend further evaluation with dedicated <10>thyroid ultrasound</10>. Diffuse low-level <11>marrow hypermetabolism</11> is nonspecific; correlate with lab values for <12>anemia</12>. tamoxifen 02/06/21 start <13>zoladex</13> 02/13/21 Start adjuvant <14>taxol</14> weekly, 12 cycles planned followed by <15>AC</15> x 4 cycles planned
