 tolerated this well. She presents today for cycle <1>8</1>.    <2>Breast cancer</2>  -right arm and hand swelling, will get <3>doppler</3> to r/o <4>DVT</4>. Discussed possibly starting on <5>anticoag</5> if positive for <6>DVT</6>. If negative for <7>DVT</7> pt will contact <8>PT</8> for <9>lymphedema</9> management.   -<10>labs</10> reviewed and adequate to receive treatment today  -Continue weekly <11>Abraxane 100mg/m2</11> x <12>12 cycles</12>. Today is week <13>8</13>.  -Continue <14>zoladex</14> for preservation of ovarian reserve during <15>chemotherapy</15>  -<16>radiation oncology referral</16>, will see Dr. ***** next week.      <17>Nausea and vomiting</17> due to <18>chemo</18> and <19>anxiety</19>, - improved   -continue ***** as premed  -Discussed more ***** use of antiemetics <20>zofran</20>, <21>compazine</21>, <22>ativan</22>.   -Continues small frequent meals.    -Continue <23>prilosec</23>.    <24>Left breast cellulitis</24>, resolved  -s/p <25>ABX</25>    <26>Birth control</26>  -ok to wait on ***** placement until after <27>chemotherapy</27>    <28>HSV</28>, <29>mouth sores/cold sores</29>  -Continue <30>valtrex 1g</30> every day throughout <31>chemo</31> as <32>ppx</32>    <33>Anxiety</33> due to diagnosis, controlled   -continue <34>lexapro</34> daily  - <35>ativan</35> prn  -Rx for <36>ambien</36> provided today.     <37>RTC 2 weeks</37>          I spent a total of <38>47 minutes</38> on this patient's care on the day of their visit excluding time spent related to any billed procedures. This time includes time spent with the patient as well as time spent documenting in the medical record, reviewing patient's records and tests, obtaining history, placing orders, communicating with other healthcare professionals, counseling the patient, family, or caregiver, and/or care coordination for the diagnoses above.            
