continues to recover from <1>surgery</1>. She met with Dr. ***** in <2>radiation oncology</2> today and elected to enrolled on a <3>clinic trial</3>, which will randomized her to 3 vs 5 weeks of <4>radiation</4>. Tentative start date is 12/16/18. We discussed the role of <5>endocrine therapy</5> today. She start an <6>aromatase inhibitor</6> after she completes radiation. She has decided to proceed with a <7>bilateral oophorectomy</7> with Dr. *****, so she may not require <8>ovarian suppression</8>. Dr. ***** also discussed she may be eligible for the ***** trial with <9>ribociclib</9> that should open around the time she completes radiation. 2. <10>Pulmonary nodule</10>: Baseline <11>PET/CT</11> in April 2018 showed a non-specific 4 mm pulmonary nodule. Her <12>CT Chest</12> in August 2018 was stable. Consider a follow up CT Chest in one year. 3. <13>Low weight</13>, improved: We encouraged her to continue efforts to gain weight. Continue small, frequent meals a day and <14>Ensure protein shakes</14>. Continue to trend weight. Follow up with <15>nutrition</15> on 11/30/18. 4. <16>Anxiety</16>: She continues to struggle with anxiety though she states this is slightly improved. Encouraged her to follow up with her local therapist. She was prescribed <17>Lexapro</17> previously but has not taken it. 5. <18>BRCA1 mutation</18>: S/p <19>bilateral mastectomy</19>. She will see Dr. ***** on 12/02/18 to discuss bilateral oophorectomy. 6. <20>Pain in neck and back</20> and <21>limited ROM in bilateral arms</21>: Referred to <22>PT</22>. Follow up on 01/05/19 This is a shared visit for services provided by me, ***** ***** *****, MD. I performed a face-to-face encounter with the patient and the following portion of the note is my own. I have reviewed the history and participated in the physical exam and assessment and plan as documented. Additional A/P: ***** looks a little stronger today and has gained a few pounds. Per the NP note, ***** will undergo a <23>BSO</23> eventually, but depending on timing, she may not need <24>OS</24> if she does not recover ovarian
