ner_results: ```plaintext
right breast, upper inner quadrant, 1:00, 1 cm from nipple. Right axilla demonstrated several enlarged <1>lymph nodes</1> with <2>cortical thickening</2> measuring up to 4 mm. There is an 11 x 11 x 9 mm right axillary node with irregular shape and indistinct margins, suspicious for <3>extranodal disease extension</3>. 12/10/2020 <4>FNA</4> of enlarged R axillary node consistent with <5>metastatic carcinoma</5> 12/23/2020 <6>MRI breast</6>: 1. A 38 mm right upper inner quadrant <7>breast mass</7> corresponds to proven <8>malignancy</8>. No evidence of <9>multifocal disease</9> or <10>contralateral malignancy</10>. Recommend continued <11>surgical</11> and <12>oncologic management</12>. 2. Right level April 26 <13>axillary adenopathy</13> corresponds to proven <14>metastatic disease</14>. 3. Nonspecific 5 mm enhancing lesion within the right upper sternum, without apparent correlate on ***** ***** of 11/11/2020. Recommend correlation with <15>bone scan</15> or <16>PET/CT</16>. 4. Suggestion of enlarged <17>mediastinal</17> and <18>hilar lymph nodes</18>, which appear more prominent in comparison to the prior <19>CT</19> of 11/11/20, although comparison is limited due to differences in technique. Suggest correlation with <20>CT</20> or <21>PET/CT</21>. 12/31/20 <22>PET/CT</22>: 1. Baseline <23>PET/CT</23> demonstrates <24>hypermetabolic right breast mass</24> consistent with known <25>invasive ductal carcinoma</25>. Associated <26>hypermetabolic right axillary</26>, <27>right internal mammary</27>, and possible <28>right anterior chest wall metastases</28>. Additional extensive <29>fat stranding</29> along the right upper extremity <30>neurovascular bundle</30> raises the possibility of <31>brachial plexus involvement</31>. 2. Extensive <32>hypermetabolic bilateral hilar</32> and <33>mediastinal lymphadenopathy</33> in a pattern most suggestive of <34>sarcoidosis</34> versus less likely <35>metastatic disease</35>. 3. *****-shaped <36>hypodensities</36> within the left greater than right <37>kidneys</37>, favoring <38>pyelonephritis</38> versus less likely developing <39>infarcts</39>. Mild circumferential <40>urinary bladder wall thickening</40> also may reflect <41>urinary tract infection</41>.
