ner_results: ```plaintext
 WRN      <1>01/14/21</1> ***** <2>abdomen</2>: 1.  No <3>MRI</3> correlate to the previously described <4>1.5 cm hypodensity</4> within the <5>left hepatic lobe</5>. The previously described <6>vascular irregularity</6> of the <7>left inferior renal artery</7> is seen, but better characterized on prior <8>CTA exam</8>.    <9>01/20/21</9> start <10>neoadjuvant taxol</10> ***** followed by *****    <11>06/02/21</11> ***** *****: <12>RIGHT Breast</12>: Interval decrease in <13>volume</13>, <14>extent</14> and <15>avidity of enhancement</15> of the known <16>right upper inner malignancy</16> with <17>residual segmental non-mass enhancement</17> measuring up to <18>28 x 10 x 25 mm</18> (AP x trans x CC extent) on <19>MIP images</19> (previously measuring up to <20>38 x 14 x 29 mm</20>).   <21>Kinetic evaluation</21> demonstrates <22>slow initial rise</22> with <23>delayed persistent enhancement</23>.  <24>Biopsy clip artifact</24> is noted along the <25>anterolateral margin</25> of the <26>non-mass enhancement</26> (axial <27>T1 non-FS image 46</27>). <28>LEFT Breast</28>: No abnormal areas of <29>enhancement</29> or other <30>MRI features of malignancy</30> are identified. <31>OTHER</31>: Decrease in size of <32>right level I and II axillary adenopathy</32> with <33>biopsy clip artifact</33> within a <34>biopsy proven nodal metastasis</34> (axial <35>T2 image 138</35>). No <36>left axillary adenopathy</36>. <37>Left chest port</37> ***** artifact.
``` 
