re-excision of <1>margins</1>. ***** send email to Dr. ***** and Dr. ***** regarding if an <2>axillary dissection</2> is recommended since she's going back to <3>surgery</3>.   -Pt's <4>port</4> was removed on <5>July 08</5> and she's worried that ***** ***** <6>site</6> is not healing as fast she she hoped. Reassured her there's no <7>s/sx of infection</7> and not concerned. Advised her to continue to monitor  -We will have her start <8>letrozole</8> now. <9>Rx</9> sent. We reviewed the potential side effects of ***** <10>therapy</10> which include but are not limited to <11>joint aches</11>, <12>hot flashes</12>, <13>dryness</13>, <14>hair thinning</14>, <15>weight gain</15>, <16>bone loss</16> and <17>increased risk of fracture</17>.  -Discussed addition of <18>abemaciclib</18> after completion of <19>xrt</19>.   -Baseline <20>dexa</20> ordered. .    -Encouraged her to fup with Dr. ***** in <21>rad onc</21> after her re-excision date is set.      <22>Granulomatous disease</22>  <23>Bronchoscopy</23> and <24>FNA</24> of <25>mediastinal nodes</25> on <26>01/09/21</26> was benign but showed <27>granulomatous disease</27> c/w <28>sarcoidosis</28>.  -Saw Dr. ***** in <29>sarcoid clinic</29> on <30>03/27/21</30>. Recommends <31>PFT</31>, <32>chest imaging</32> and <33>sarcoid related blood tests</33>.  -Saw <34>rheumatology</34> on <35>06/22/21</35> who did not feel she had any <36>systemic autoimmune disease</36>  -Fup with Dr. ***** and Dr. *****     <37>Joint pain</37>, <38>chronic</38>, improve  -unclear etiology, ?<39>sarcoidosis</39>. Saw <40>rheumatology</40> who did not feel she has any <41>systemic autoimmune disease</41>.   -Continue <42>naproxen 500mg bid</42>, <43>APAP</43> ok if taken sparingly  -Discussed <44>tramadol</44> if pain worsens/uncontrolled  -Discussed <45>PT</45> in the past       <46>Aneurysm of the distal renal artery</46>  -Seen on <47>CT abd angiogram</47> in <48>December 2020</48>  Saw Dr. ***** ***** <49>vascular surgery</49> on <50>01/26/21</50>. Does not rec <51>surgical intervention</51>. Her <52>renal artery u/s</52> was normal although she had <53>coffee</53> <54>AM</54> - unclear if that effects these results. If visualized, then <55>surveillance u/s imaging</55> in <56>1 year</56>. Since not visualized, will obtain <57>MRA of the abdomen</57> in <58>1 year</58> as well, due in <59>January 2022</59>  -Fup with Dr. *****     <60>Myalgias</60> likely due to <61>chemo</61>, unchanged   -Continue <62>naproxen 500mg BID</62>
