ner_results: ```plaintext
 immediately adjacent to the previously described <1>complex solid and cystic mass</1>, there is a <2>2.8 x 1.8 x 2.6 cm simple cyst</2>.  Corresponding to the <3>mass in the right breast on mammogram</3>, in the inner central right breast, at the 9 o'clock position <4>3 cm</4> the nipple, there is a <5>conglomerate of simple cysts</5> measuring up to <6>1.1 cm</6>.  <7>Benign appearing lymph nodes</7> are seen in both axillae.    IMPRESSION:   <8>Left breast: Highly suggestive of malignancy (BI-RADS 5)</8>.  <9>Right breast: Benign (BI-RADS 2)</9>.    <10>06/12/17 path core</10>  FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS    <11>Left breast, ultrasound-guided core biopsy</11>: <12>Scant detached fragments of carcinoma with necrosis and calcifications</12>    <13>07/05/17 mri</13>  MRI Findings:  This <14>bilateral breast MRI exam</14> demonstrates <15>mild background enhancement</15>.  There are <16>scattered areas of fibroglandular tissue</16>.    RIGHT Breast:  <17>No abnormal areas of enhancement or other MRI features of malignancy</17> are identified.    LEFT Breast:  There is a <18>heterogeneous 23 anteroposterior x 23 transverse x 24 craniocaudal mm (axial post contrast image 47/*****, sagittal reformat image 118/*****) oval mass</18> with <19>irregular margins and rim enhancement</19> in the inner central left breast. ***** <20>intensity/time curve</20> demonstrates <21>rapid initial rise and washout enhancement kinetics</21>.  Extending anterolateral from the <22>index malignancy</22> is <23>non-mass enhancement with clumped internal enhancement</23>, with a <24>total extent of disease measuring 31 mm (axial post contrast image 52/***** of series 2)</24>.    IMPRESSION:   <25>Left breast: Known biopsy proven malignancy (BI-RADS 6)</25>.  <26>Right breast: Negative (BI-RADS 1)</26>.    <27>July 06 bx</27>:  FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS    <28>Left breast, ultrasound-guided core biopsy</28>:   1. <29>At least ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate nuclear grade</29>; see  comment.  2. <30>Biopsy site changes and necrosis</30>.  3. <31>Microcalcifications with stroma and as detached fragments</31>.       COMMENT:  The biopsy consists mostly of <32>granulation tissue</32>, <33>foamy</33>
``` 
