ner_results: ```plaintext
12:00 position, 7 cm from the nipple with extension posteriorly to the pectoralis muscle without muscle involvement. In addition, in the upper inner <1>left breast</1>, middle third, there was a bilobed enhancing <2>nodule</2> (1 cm), located 5 cm from the nipple, and 3 cm from the chest wall. A <3>lymph node</3> (2.5 cm) was present in the <4>left axilla</4> with associated clip as well as additional prominent asymmetric <5>left axillary LN</5>. The <6>right breast</6> was notable for scattered <7>cysts</7>, but no suspicious enhancing masses. She then underwent a <8>left breast US</8> to look at the <9>MRI-findings</9> at the 12:00 position demonstrated an area of <10>hypoechogenicity</10> (2.3 cm). A <11>left breast US-guided core biopsy</11> at the 12:00 position was notable for <12>invasive ductal carcinoma</12> with <13>ER+</13> (100%), <14>PR+</14> (100%), *****- (<15>IHC 2+</15>; <16>FISH ratio 1.4</16>). A <17>left breast US</17> to look at the <18>MRI-findings</18> at the 10:00 position demonstrated a vague <19>hypoechoic area</19>. A <20>left breast US-guided core biopsy</20> at the 10:00 position was notable for <21>invasive ductal carcinoma</21>, also with <22>ER+</22> (100%), <23>PR+</23> (100%), *****- (<24>IHC 0</24>). This <25>biopsy</25> was sent for ***** and resulted as <26>low risk</26> with a <27>score of 11</27>. She underwent a <28>PET with CT</28> for attenuation purposes on 11/22/16 demonstrated no uptake in known <29>left axillary LN metastasis</29> or in the <30>left breast</30>, however, uptake in the <31>bone marrow</31> of <32>T7-L1</32> was slightly more prominent, of unclear significance. A <33>thoracic spine MRI</33> on 12/07/16 was notable for no evidence of <34>metastases</34>. She has met with Dr. ***** ***** in ***** ***** who recommended <35>neoadjuvant dose-dense AC</35> followed by <36>paclitaxel</36> as well as Dr. ***** at ***** ***** ***** who recommended proceeding with <37>surgical resection</37> first to assess extent of <38>disease</38>. Today patient also met with Drs. ***** and ***** regarding <39>L breast mastectomy</39> and <40>reconstruction</40> and has scheduled her <41>surgery</41> for 01/06/17. She had prior <42>biopsies</42> in both breasts several years ago which patient reports
``` 
