ner_results: ```plaintext
<1>Peripheral neuropathy</1>: Although uncommon, a serious side effect of decreased sensation and <2>paresthesia</2> (numbness and tingling of the extremities) may be noted. <3>Sensory loss</3>, numbness and tingling, and difficulty in walking may last for at least as long as therapy is continued. These side effects may become progressively more severe with continued treatment, and your doctor may decide to decrease your dose. <4>Central neurotoxicity</4>: Infrequent but patients over age 65 are at increased risk. Symptoms include <5>dizziness</5>, <6>confusion</6>, <7>visual changes</7>, <8>ringing in the ears</8>. <9>Nephrotoxicity</9> (see <10>kidney problems</10>): More frequent when <11>Carboplatin</11> is given in high doses or to people with kidney problems. <12>Hearing loss</12> (<13>ototoxicity</13>) - loss of high pitched sounds. <14>Abnormal blood electrolyte levels</14> (<15>sodium</15>, <16>potassium</16>, <17>calcium</17>). <18>Abnormal blood liver enzymes</18> (<19>SGOT</19>, <20>Alkaline phosphatase</20>) (see <21>liver problems</21>). <22>Cardiovascular events</22>. Although infrequent, <23>heart failure</23>, <24>blood clots</24> and <25>strokes</25> have been reported with <26>Carboplatin</26> use. Less than 1% were life-threatening. <27>Allergic reaction</27> may occur. It would occur during the actual transfusion. This may include <28>itching</28>, <29>rash</29>, <30>shortness of breath</30> or <31>dizziness</31> (especially in patients who have received <32>cisplatin</32>). Not all side effects are listed above, some that are rare (occurring in less than 10% of patients) are not listed here. However, you should always inform your health care provider if you experience any unusual symptoms. Use of <33>anti-emetics</33> and other drug specific instructions reviewed: Reviewed with pt on anti-emetics <34>Zofran</34> <35>Ativan</35> <36>Compazine</36> Other topics reviewed: [x] How to communicate with us [x] When to contact us [x] When to obtain labs [x] Additional support services available: The Patient and Family Cancer Support Center (formerly the Cancer Resource Center): *****://*****.*****.*****/*****/*****/, <37>Social worker</37>
``` 
