ner_results: ```plaintext
management recommendations were discussed at length with ***** and her two sisters who were present. ***** has undergone the <1>surgical resection</1> of her <2>left breast tumor</2> with <3>SLN assessment</3> as well. It is likely that she has additional <4>LNs with metastatic disease</4>. This is estimated to be about 64% by the <5>MSKCC normogram</5> and 44% by the ***** normogram. The role of <6>axillary dissection</6> and its pros/cons have been discussed with her by Dr. *****. ***** remains with a considerable risk of systemic relapse and mortality from this <7>cancer</7>. Although the most accurate risk assessment is not possible without quantitative <8>LN data</8> from an <9>axillary dissection</9>, her risk is clearly high. I estimate her risk to be on the order of 60% or higher. This can be reduced with the use of <10>adjuvant chemotherapy</10>, *****-targeting therapy, <11>hormonal therapy</11>, <12>radiotherapy</12>, and <13>bisphosphonate therapy</13>. These modalities were discussed. ***** will benefit from <14>adjuvant systemic chemotherapy</14>. Recommendation was made for <15>adjuvant AC/THP chemotherapy</15>. This consists of <16>AC x 4</16> given q2weeks with <17>growth factor support</17>, followed by 12 weeks of <18>taxol</18> along with one year of <19>trastuzumab</19> and <20>pertuzumab</20>. Side effects were discussed including potential for <21>nausea/vomiting</21>, <22>alopecia</22>, <23>bone marrow suppression</23> and <24>infections</24>, <25>cardiomyopathy</25>, <26>neuropathy</26>, and a small risk of <27>secondary leukemias</27>. As an alternative, we also discussed the <28>TCHP regimen</28>. This consists of 6 cycles of <29>TCHP</29> with one year of <30>trastuzumab/pertuzumab</30>. Side effects are similar with sparing of the <31>cardiomyopathy</31> and <32>leukemogenic risks</32>. We also discussed the use of <33>extended adjuvant neratinib</33> in year 2 including the potential for <34>diarrhea</34> and the need for prophylactic anti-*****. ***** will also benefit from <35>adjuvant hormone therapy</35>. A recommendation was made for <36>Arimidex 1 mg PO daily</36> for a duration of 10 years. This would begin at the completion of <37>chemotherapy</37>. Side effects were discussed.
