fasting and a suitable delay of 60 minutes following the intravenous administration of <1>15.63 mCi 18F-FDG</1> at the right hand, <2>3D body imaging</2> is performed from the base of the skull to below the pelvis using the <3>General Electric Discovery ST PET/CT scanner</3>. Initially, a <4>low dose CT</4> is performed for <5>attenuation correction</5> and <6>anatomic correlation</6>. Subsequent <7>3.0 minute bed positions</7> were then performed for acquisition of the <8>PET data set</8> with subsequent fusion with the <9>CT</9> for the <10>diagnostic data set</10>. The patient's <11>blood glucose</11> at the time of injection was <12>88 mg/dL</12>. RADIATION DOSIMETRY: <13>CTDIvol</13>: <14>5.6 mGy</14> Total exam <15>DLP</15>: <16>497.85 mGy-cm</16> COMPARISON: <17>Pelvic ultrasound</17> from <18>10/23/2008</18>. FINDINGS: The distribution of <19>18F-FDG</19> in the visualized <20>brain</20>, <21>myocardium</21> and the <22>urinary tract</22> appears physiologic. Head and neck: There is no hypermetabolic deep <23>cervical lymphadenopathy</23>. Thorax: There is a <24>hypermetabolic mass</24> in the outer quadrant of the <25>left breast</25> with associated <26>clip</26>. The mass is <27>isodense</27> to the adjacent glandular tissue, measuring approximately <28>2.2 x 1.8 cm</28> with maximum <29>SUV 3.4</29>. Additional note is made of <30>2 enlarged hypermetabolic left axillary lymph node</30>. The larger and more hypermetabolic lymph node measures <31>10 mm</31> in short axis dimension with maximum <32>SUV 4.2</32>. No enlarged right metabolic <33>internal mammary lymph nodes</33> are identified. No hypermetabolic hilar or <34>mediastinal lymphadenopathy</34> is present. There are no <35>pulmonary nodules</35> or <36>pleural effusions</36>. The <37>heart size</37> appears normal. There is a <38>trace pericardial effusion</38>. Abdomen and pelvis: There are no hypermetabolic lesions in the <39>liver</39>, <40>adrenal glands</40> or <41>retroperitoneal lymph nodes</41>. There is a small non-FDG avid low-density lesion in <42>hepatic</42> *****, likely a <43>cyst</43>, measuring <44>7 mm</44>. The <45>uterus</45> is prominent in size. There is focal linear uptake within the right side of the uterus with maximum <46>SUV 4.5</46>.
