 corresponding abnormality is difficult to visualize on the   noncontrast images.    Musculoskeletal: <1>Spondylotic changes</1> are present within the <2>spinal axis</2>. There are no   hypermetabolic or osteolytic <3>bone metastases</3>.    IMPRESSION:   1. <4>Hypermetabolic mass</4> in the outer quadrant of the <5>left breast</5>, consistent with known <6>breast cancer</6>.  2. <7>Hypermetabolic left axillary lymph nodes</7>, consistent with <8>nodal metastatic disease</8>.  3. Somewhat linear abnormal uptake eccentric lesion within the <9>right side of the uterus</9>. A   corresponding abnormality difficult to determine on the noncontrast images. This could relate   to uptake within the <10>endometrial canal</10> that is displaced, which can be seen physiologically in   patients of reproductive age. Alternately, this could represent uptake in the <11>endometrial canal</11>   due to <12>inflammatory change</12> in this patient status post recent <13>IUD removal</13>. However, the   eccentric nature of the uptake is atypical for <14>endometrial uptake</14>. Recommend a <15>pelvic   ultrasound</15> for initial further evaluation to ensure that this does not correspond with a   <16>uterine mass</16>.      <17>05/31/19</17>: <18>Brain MRI</18>:      Technique:     <19>Diffusion axial</19>  <20>Axial T2 FLAIR</20>  <21>Axial T2 fast spin-echo</21>  <22>Sagittal T1 FLAIR</22>  <23>Gradient echo axial</23>  <24>T1-weighted axial</24>    Contrast enhanced sequences: None  Contrast dose: <25>6 ml IV Gadavist</25>.    Findings:  <26>Brain parenchyma</26>: The <27>ventricles</27> and <28>extra-axial CSF spaces</28> are normal. There is no evidence   of <29>intra-axial mass</29>, <30>acute mass effect</30> or <31>bleed</31>.  Major intracranial vascular structures. No <32>aneurysm</32>, unremarkable.  <33>Sinuses/Mastoid air cells</33>: Clear  <34>Pituitary</34>: The configuration of the <35>sella</35> is normal.  <36>Orbits</36>: Unremarkable.  *****: Unremarkable       Impression:   No evidence of <37>acute infarction</37> or suspicious enhancing <38>masses</38>.       <39>09/02/19</39>: <40>Breast MRI</40>:    CLINICAL INDICATION:  <41>Malignant neoplasm</41> of <42>lower-outer quadrant of left female breast</42>,   <43>unspecified estrogen receptor status</43> (CMS/HCC).
