CLINICAL DIAGNOSIS AND HISTORY:  Hx <1>invasive carcinoma</1>, <2>left breast</2>, <3>3:30 N+3</3>; S/P <4>neoadjuvant chemotherapy</4> (by report).    DIAGNOSIS:  A. <5>LEFT BREAST</5>; <6>PARTIAL MASTECTOMY</6> (WIRE LOCALIZATION):  -  <7>INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA</7>, <8>GRADE II</8>; <9>TUMOR</9> MEASURING  <10>38 X 35 MM</10> (SEE COMMENT).  -  <11>DUCTAL CARCINOMA</11> ***** ***** (<12>DCIS</12>), <13>INTERMEDIATE TO HIGH-GRADE</13>, FOCAL.  -  LOCALIZED ORGANIZING <14>FIBROHISTIOCYTIC</14> AND ***** <15>CELL BIOPSY SITE REACTION</15>.  -  BACKGROUND <16>BREAST TISSUE</16> WITH <17>STROMAL FIBROSIS</17> AND  FOCAL MILD <18>NONPROLIFERATIVE FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES</18>.    B. <19>LATERAL MARGIN</19>, <20>LEFT BREAST</20>; <21>EXCISION</21>:  -  <22>INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA</22>; <23>TUMOR</23> MEASURING <24>8.0 X 6.0 MM</24>.  -  ***** <25>INVASION</25> IDENTIFIED.    C. <26>ANTERIOR (SUPERFICIAL) MARGIN</26>, <27>LEFT BREAST</27>; <28>EXCISION</28>:  -  <29>INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA</29>; <30>TUMOR</30> MEASURING <31>25 X 15 MM</31>.  -  ***** <32>INVASION</32> IDENTIFIED.    D. <33>LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE</33>; <34>EXCISION</34>:  -  <35>METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA</35> ***** ***** ***** <36>NODE</36> (February 06);  <37>METASTATIC TUMOR</37> MEASURING <38>15 MM</38> IN *****.    E. <39>LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODES #2</39>; <40>EXCISION</40>:  -  <41>MICROMETASTATIC CARCINOMA</41> ***** ***** ***** <42>TWO LYMPH NODES</42>  (February 07), with DEPOSITS OF <43>TUMOR</43> MEASURING BETWEEN <44>1.0 AND <2.0 MM</44>; in addition to <45>isolated tumor cells</45> in both nodes,  as well as <46>extranodal tumor infiltrating adipose tissue</46>.
