- 07/31/20: Bilateral <12>breast MRI</12>: <13>Right breast, 7:00, N+4cm</13>: In total, the abnormal enhancement spans <14>6 cm AP</14> by <15>3.3 cm</15> ***** by <16>2.8 cm</16>. In the <17>right breast 6:00</17>, 8 cm from the nipple, there is a <18>1.4 x 0.8 x 0.7 cm irregular mass</18> with associated <19>biopsy marker</19> abutting or extending to the overlying skin. A <20>2.2 cm area of skin thickening and enhancement</20> the <21>right breast 9 to 10:00 position</21>, 6 cm from the nipple. There are <22>2 prominent low right axillary lymph nodes</22> with possible cortical thickening. <23>Left breast negative</23>.     
07/26/20:   
A. <24>Breast, right 7:00 N+4, core</24>
