ner_results: ```plaintext
administered in the adjuvant or neoadjuvant settings with equivalent benefits on long term outcomes outcomes (***** ***** *****; ***** ***** *****; ***** ***** *****). However there are certain advantages to the neoadjuvant timing. These include the opportunity to confirm the in ***** response, the powerful prognostic information provided by pathologic response status (***** ***** *****; ***** ***** *****; ***** ***** *****; ***** ***** *****; ***** ***** *****), and the opportunity for salvage therapies or clinical trials should there be extensive residual <1>disease</1> after <2>neoadjuvant chemotherapy</2> ***** a high risk of relapse. She has already started on <3>neo-adjuvant AC/taxol chemotherapy</3> and I concurred with this (***** ***** *****; ***** ***** *****). This consists of 4 cycles of <4>AC</4> at <5>60/600 mg/m2</5> given every 2 weeks with <6>growth factor support</6> followed by <7>taxol</7> given either in 4 doses of <8>175mg/m2</8> q2weeks or in 12 weekly doses of <9>80mg/m2</9>. Side effects were discussed including a potential for <10>nausea</10>, <11>vomiting</11>, <12>alopecia</12>, <13>immune suppression</13> and <14>infections</14>, <15>fatigue</15>, <16>neuropathy</16>. Long term sequelae include 1-2% incidence of <17>cardiomyopathy</17> (***** ***** *****; ***** ***** *****) and 0.5% incidence of <18>secondary myeloid neoplasms</18> (***** ***** *****). ***** will be having <19>surgery</19> after the completion of <20>neo-adjuvant chemotherapy</20>. Considering her <21>locally advanced disease</21>, it may be wise to perform an <22>axillary dissection</22>, and if feasible, to identify and remove the <23>subpectoral LNs</23> as well. The feasibility of this is best determined by ***** and may require a repeat <24>scan</24> post-chemo to determine the extent of residual macroscopic <25>disease</25>. ***** refer to ***** at ***** should she wish to pursue <26>surgery</26> here. ***** will benefit from <27>adjuvant hormonal therapy</27> for a duration of up to 10 years. Both <28>tamoxifen</28> and <29>AIs</29> are effective with <30>AIs</30> showing superior efficacy.
``` 
