ner_results: ```plaintext
 in randomized trials (***** ***** *****)(***** ***** *****). Side effects of <1>tamoxifen</1> were discussed including potential for <2>hot flashes</2>, <3>mood effects</3>, increased incidence of <4>thromboembolic events</4> and <5>endometrial cancer</5> in postmenopausal women. Side effects of <6>AIs</6> were discussed including *****, <7>myalgias</7>, and potential acceleration of <8>bone loss</8>. Although <9>AIs</9> are restricted to the postmenopausal state, ***** has <10>high risk disease</10> and will benefit from the superior efficacy afforded by <11>AIs</11>. This was confirmed in the combined analysis of the <12>SOFT</12> and <13>TEXT trials</13> wherein <14>ovarian suppression</14> with <15>aromatase inhibitor therapy</15> was the optimal <16>hormonal therapy</16> modality in premenopausal patients (***** ***** *****). ***** will likely be <17>peri-menopausal</17> at the completion of <18>chemotherapy</18> and may require <19>ovarian suppression</19> for a period of time. Alternatively ***** therapy with continuous <20>estradiol monitoring</20> for a period of time may establish a permanent <21>menopausal status</21> without the need for suppression. The <22>bone loss</22> associated with postmenopausal use of <23>AIs</23> can be ***** with <24>anti-resorptive bone agents</24>. In addition to beneficial effects on bone, the use of ***** or <25>denosumab</25> every 6 months for 3 years in post-menopausal patients with early stage <26>breast cancer</26> is associated with a significant reduction in <27>breast cancer recurrence</27> (***** ***** ***** ***** ***** ***** *****), providing additional benefit to their use in this patient population. Side effects of <28>zoledronic acid</28> and <29>denosumab</29> were discussed including a rare risk of ***** with no cases confirmed in the *****-12 or *****-18 studies (***** ***** ***** ***** ***** ***** *****), but 2% in the more intense schedule of the ***** trial (***** ***** *****), and a rare risk of <30>atypical femoral fractures</30> at a rate of under 0.2% (***** ***** *****) with no cases confirmed in the *****-18 study (***** ***** *****). <31>Zoledronic infusions</31>
``` 
