to the available <1>mammogram report</1>, <2>PET/CT report</2>, and the <3>pathology report</3> describing findings of <4>carcinoma</4> in April 30 <5>biopsied LNs</5> as well as associated <6>tumor grade</6> and <7>receptor status</7> as above. Overall, based on a primary <8>tumor size</8> of 2.1cm, high <9>tumor grade</9>, involvement of <10>axillary lymph nodes</10>, <11>receptor status</11>, and lack of evidence of <12>metastatic spread</12>, this <13>cancer</13> is a <14>stage II-III</14> (*****-3fM0), pending <15>axillary LN analysis</15> on resection. We next discussed <16>treatment</16>. In general it has been thought that <17>neoadjuvant chemotherapy</17> may offer the opportunity to downstage a <18>tumor</18> prior to resection and thus facilitate <19>breast conservation</19>, with no difference in ***** or <20>OS</20> vs ***** surgery. However, new evidence is emerging regarding the efficacy of <21>adjuvant ***** targeted therapy</21> in the setting of <22>residual disease</22> after <23>neoadjuvant treatment</23> (***** 2019;380:617-28), with improved <24>DFS</24> and a trend towards improved <25>OS</25>. Therefore, we recommend <26>neoadjuvant treatment</26>. There are multiple reasonable regimens, although we suggest <27>TCHP</27> (<28>docetaxel</28> and <29>carboplatin</29> every 3 weeks for 6 cycles with concurrent ***** and <30>pertuzumab</30>) or ***** (weekly <31>paclitaxel</31> with <32>carboplatin</32>, administered every three weeks or weekly, with concurrent <33>trastuzumab</33> and <34>pertuzumab</34>). <35>Adjuvant treatment</35> selection will be guided by an assessment of <36>tumor response</36> at resection, including the potential option ***** cycles of *****-***** <37>emtansine</37> if there is not a complete response to <38>neoadjuvant therapy</38>. We briefly discussed <39>treatment side effects</39> including <40>hair loss</40>, <41>nausea/vomiting</41>, <42>diarrhea</42>, and risk of <43>infection</43>, but left a full discussion for formal <44>chemotherapy teaching</44>. We also discussed the need for <45>radiation therapy</45> and <46>surgical resection</46>. We will refer Ms. ***** to the <47>UCSF Breast Surgery clinic</47> for consultation regarding <48>surgical resection</48>. Following <49>surgical resection</49> we will plan to refer Ms. ***** to <50>Radiation Oncology</50>.
