of 28 day cycle  09/07/18 Hold C6 OPERA with <1>***** 300 mg BID</1> <2>D1, 8, 15 of 28 day cycle</2> due to persistent <3>headaches</3>  09/14/18 dose reduced <4>***** ***** ***** 200 mg/m2 (250 mg) BID</4> due to <5>fatigue</5> and <6>failure to thrive</6>  10/04/18 <7>PET/CT</7> showed mild to interval increase in <8>***** avidity</8> and peripheral soft tissue within the indexed <9>hepatic metastasis</9>; however, overall size remains stable. When compared to prior <10>PET/CT</10> from 08/09/2018, interval decreased <11>FDG uptake</11> in <12>portacaval nodal metastases</12> without significant change in size.   10/12/18  dose reduced <13>***** ***** ***** 200 mg/m2 (250 mg) BID</13>  11/29/18 <14>PET/CT</14>: New <15>left para-aortic lymph node</15> and increased size of <16>portacaval nodal conglomerate</16>, as well as mildly increased size of centrally necrotic <17>liver metastasis</17>. No other hypermetabolic metastatic disease.    12/29/18 <18>CT CAP</18>: <19>Hepatic segment 8 centrally necrotic lesion</19> is larger compared to most recent prior from 11/29/2018, now measuring <20>3.1 x 4.8 cm</20> compared to <21>2.7 x 3.4 cm</21>. Similar appearance of <22>portacaval nodal conglomerate</22> moderate measuring approximately <23>4.1 x 4.5 cm</23>. There are multiple new <24>*****</24> and <25>periaortic lymph nodes</25> measuring up to <26>1.0 cm</26>.  12/29/18 <27>MRI brain</27>: Stable large <28>pontine cavernous malformation</28>, with sequela of prior <29>hemorrhage</29> in the dorsal left pons.    12/31/18 <30>***** ***** Panel</30>: Pathogenic or likely pathogenic <31>SOMATIC ALTERATION</31> ( <32>CDK</32>, <33>*****</33>, <34>EPHA7</34>)    01/03/19 to 03/15/19 - received 4 cycles of <35>gemcitabine</35>    02/08/19 <36>a/p CT</36> showed decreased size of <37>metastatic disease</37> involving the <38>liver</38> and <39>periportal lymph nodes</39>. <40>Distention of the endometrial cavity</40> with heterogeneous material, which is unchanged compared to priors and was not hypermetabolic on prior <41>PET</41>. <42>Chest CT</42> showed no <43>intrathoracic metastatic disease</43>. 03/22/19 <44>a/c/p CT</44> - further mild decrease in size of multiple <45>hepatic metastatic lesions</45> as well as mild improvement in <46>periportal nodal conglomerate</46>. Unchanged <47>distention</47> of
