Part 1. Left breast, <1>needle-localized partial mastectomy</1>.  1.  <2>Residual invasive ductal carcinoma</2> adjacent to <3>biopsy site</3>, modified  ***** grade 1, 0.3 cm (slide 1N deeper recut), <4>margins negative</4>.  2.  <5>Invasive lobular carcinoma</5>, modified ***** grade 1, at least 0.2 cm  (slides 1B and 1P), <6>margins negative</6>; see comment.  3.  <7>Ductal carcinoma in situ</7>, low nuclear grade, cribriform pattern with  focal necrosis; see comment.  4.  <8>Atypical ductal hyperplasia</8>.  5.  <9>Atypical lobular hyperplasia</9>.  6.  <10>Proliferative fibrocystic changes</10>, including <11>usual ductal hyperplasia</11>, <12>sclerosing adenosis</12>, <13>columnar cell change/hyperplasia</13>, <14>apocrine metaplasia</14> and <15>microcysts</15>.  7.  <16>Biopsy site changes</16>.  8.  <17>Calcifications</17> associated with <18>ductal carcinoma in situ</18>, <19>atypical ductal hyperplasia</19> and <20>benign ducts</20>.  9.  <21>Benign skin</21>.    

Part 2. Left breast tissue, <22>mastopexy</22>:  1.  <23>Benign breast tissue</23> with <24>apocrine metaplasia</24> and <25>calcifications</25> in <26>benign ducts</26>.  2.  <27>Benign skin</27>.  3.  <28>Dense fibrous tissue</28> consistent with <29>implant capsule</29>.    

Part 3. Left axillary <30>sentinel lymph node</30>, <31>excision</31>:
``` 
