ner_results: ```plaintext
ninth rib. These prior findings were equivocal, with limited, treated/resolved (by metabolism) <1>skeletal metastatic disease</1> not entirely excluded. However, there is currently felt to be no definitive metabolic evidence of active <2>skeletal metastatic disease</2>. For reference/comparison purposes, <3>blood pool activity</3> within the <4>descending thoracic aorta</4> (at the level of the carina) demonstrates an approximate <5>SUV</5> of <6>2.0</6> currently and <7>2.2</7> previously. Other Result Information Ifc, ***** Amb ***** Results In - *****/*****/***** *****:***** PM PST PROCEDURE: <8>PET SKULL BASE MID THIGH W ATTENUATION CT</8> ***** *****, *****/*****/***** *****:***** PM STUDY: <9>F-18 FDG Whole Body PET/CT Study</9> CLINICAL INDICATION: 77-year-old woman with a history of <10>right breast invasive lobular carcinoma</10> with <11>right axillary nodal metastatic involvement</11>, treated with <12>letrozole</12> (since December 2019). <13>Restaging evaluation/assessment of response to therapy</13>. COMPARISON: Prior <14>PET/CT</14> at ***** ***** ***** Imaging Center on <15>10/31/2019</15>. A <16>CT of the chest, abdomen, and pelvis</16> on <17>12/06/2019</17> and a <18>whole body bone scan</18> on <19>11/21/2019</19> are also reviewed. TECHNIQUE: At the time of this study, the patient's <20>fasting blood glucose</20> was <21>93 mg/dL</21> and her <22>weight</22> was <23>199 lbs</23>. Approximately <24>70 minutes</24> after the intravenous administration of <25>12.0 mCi of 18-FDG</25>, <26>PET emission images</26> and <27>CT (dose-limited, without CT contrast) transmission images</27> were acquired from the top of the head to the mid thighs. The <28>PET images</28> were subsequently corrected for <29>tissue attenuation</29>, fused with the <30>CT images</30>, and reconstructed for review in orthogonal and <31>3D rotating (MIP) projections</31>. (<32>CT dose information</32>: <33>CTDIvol</33> = <34>9.9 mGy</34>, <35>DLP</35> = <36>956.50 mGy-cm</36>) FINDINGS: Head and Neck: There is relatively symmetric physiologic <37>brain activity</37> (though evaluation of the brain on this study is limited). There is physiologic <38>tonsillar</38>, <39>salivary gland</39>, and <40>oral activity</40>.
``` 
