effect or midline shift. Diffuse <1>osseous metastases</1> throughout the <2>calvarium</2>. Stable findings of <3>demyelinating disease</3>.  11/07/20: <4>MRI brain</4>: Stable <5>demyelinating disease</5> since 09/29/2020. No active lesions. Stable diffuse <6>osseous metastases</6>. Diffuse irregular ***** enhancement along the bilateral <7>cerebral convexities</7> and right <8>petroclival region</8>, and nodular enhancement filling the right *****'s ***** is again seen and unchanged compared to 09/29/2020. This is presumed to represent <9>metastatic disease</9>. Since that study, there is increased involvement of the right <10>internal auditory canal</10>       *****, ***** reports that starting in late August, she developed <11>decreased vision</11> in her right eye. She reports <12>double vision</12> with gaze in certain positions. 3-4 weeks ago she also lost <13>hearing</13> in her right ear. Most recently, she developed <14>dizziness</14>, prompting an <15>ED visit</15> on 11/07/20. <16>MRI brain</16> showed that compared to an <17>MRI brain</17> from 09/29/20, there was largely unchanged ***** enhancement along the bilateral <18>cerebral convexities</18> and right <19>petroclival region</19>. The report did describe possible increase thickening in the right <20>internal auditory canal</20>.     She also has a history of <21>MS</21>, which was initially diagnosed in 1985. ***** reports that her <22>MS</22> presented with <23>optic neuritis</23> and <24>loss of vision</24> in her right eye. The <25>optic neuritis</25> resolved and her right eye vision has improved since that time. She has been <26>wheelchair-bound</26> since 2002 or 2003. She has been on <27>Avonex (interferon beta 1a)</27> for many years and she reports that her <28>MS</28> has been largely stable.    <29>ROS</29>: <30>Vision and hearing changes</30> per <31>HPI</31>.  GEN: No <32>fevers</32>, <33>chills</33>, <34>unintentional weight loss</34>, <35>night sweats</35>  HEENT: No  <36>icterus</36>,  <37>sore throat</37>, <38>voice changes</38>, <39>swallowing problems</39>, <40>sinus problems</40>, <41>headache</41>  NECK: No <42>neck mass</42> or <43>pain</43>, <44>swelling</44>  CV: No <45>chest pain</45>, <46>palpitations</46>, <47>murmur</47>, <48>light headed</48>, <49>edema</49>  RESP: No <50>shortness of breath</50>, <51>dyspnea on exertion</51>
