patent. There is conventional <44>hepatic arterial anatomy</44>. No <45>splenomegaly</45>. Subtle areas of heterogeneity within the mid <46>pancreas</46>, possibly related to contrast bolus timing with underlying <47>mass lesions</47> not excluded. Normal <48>pancreas</48> without <49>duct dilatation</49>, <50>atrophy</50>, or <51>focal mass lesions</51>. The <52>adrenal glands</52> are
