<1>radiation oncology</1> for consideration of <2>radiation therapy</2> (either just to her <3>internal auditory canal</3> or to a larger portion of her *****). We would also consider starting <4>low dose steroids</4> to see if this improves her <5>symptoms</5>. In terms of future options, if a <6>CT CAP</6> shows clear progression on <7>Xeloda</7>, we would consider another <8>hormone-based therapy</8> strategy. We would consider <9>fulvestrant</9> plus the ***** <10>inhibitor</10> ***** (*****) (***** ***** 2019), given her known ***** mutation on <11>Strata testing</11>. In this study, in the cohort of patients with *****-mutated cancer, progression-free survival at a median follow-up of 20 months was 11.0 months in the *****-<12>fulvestrant</12> group, as compared with 5.7 months in the placebo-<13>fulvestrant</13> group. However, this regimen does not have great <14>CNS penetration</14>, but there are few regimens that do. Given that she has <15>metastatic disease</15> to the <16>bone</16>, we agree with continuing <17>zolendronic acid</17> Recommendations: -- Repeat <18>CT CAP</18> now -- Repeat <19>LP</19> for <20>CSF cytology</20> -- Repeat <21>MRI spine</21> to r/o <22>LMD</22> in the <23>spine</23> -- Recommend referral to <24>radiation oncology</24> to consider either focal <25>CNS radiation</25> or possible even *****. The patient is interested in a <26>UCSF Rad Onc opinion</26> as well. -- Could consider starting <27>low dose steroids</27> to see if reduction of swelling improves any of her <28>symptoms</28> -- Continue <29>Xeloda 1500mg BID</29> for now -- At time of progression of <30>disease</30>, could consider <31>fulvestrant</31> + ***** given the ***** mutation on <32>STRATA testing</32> -- Continue <33>zolendronic acid</33> Patient seen and discussed with <34>breast oncology</34> attending *****. ***** *****. ***** *****, MD PGY-5 <35>Hematology/Oncology Fellow</35>
