<1>differentiated breast carcinoma</1> (SGS-20-3979). This <2>cerebellar tumor resection</2> shows <3>poorly differentiated adenocarcinoma</3> composed of nests and sheets of large pleomorphic epithelioid cells, with zones of <4>geographic necrosis</4>. <5>Immunohistochemistry</5> (block A1) with <6>GATA3 antibody</6> is positive, supportive of <7>breast origin</7>. <8>Immunohistochemistry</8> (block A1) with <9>ER</9> and <10>PR</10> is negative, although the <11>primary tumor</11> was reported as weakly positive for both. <12>Bilateral mastectomy</12> and <13>right sentinel</13> and <14>left ALND</14> August 2019 CASE: *****-*****-***** PATIENT: ***** ***** CLINICAL DATA: <15>MALIGNANT NEOPLASM OF LOWER-OUTER QUADRANT OF LEFT FEMALE BREAST</15> (CMS/HCC) [*****.511] SPECIMEN: A. <16>RIGHT BREAST</16> B. <17>RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE</17> C. <18>LEFT BREAST WITH AXILLARY CONTENTS</18> DIAGNOSIS: A. <19>RIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY</19>: 1. SKIN, ***** AND <20>BREAST TISSUE</20> WITH NO SPECIFIC ABNORMALITY. 2. NEGATIVE FOR <21>CARCINOMA</21>. B. <22>RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, BIOPSY</22>: <23>ONE LYMPH NODE</23>, NEGATIVE FOR <24>CARCINOMA</24> (O/1). C. <25>LEFT BREAST WITH AXILLARY CONTENTS, MASTECTOMY</25>: 1. <26>MULTIFOCAL INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA</26> OF NO SPECIFIC TYPE (<27>DUCTAL, NOT OTHERWISE SPECIFIED</27>). - <28>TWO FOCI</28> IDENTIFIED, MEASURING 4.0 AND 2.6 CM IN ***** DIMENSION. - <29>HISTOLOGIC GRADE: III/III</29> (SCORE: 3+3+3=January 17) BY MODIFIED ***** CRITERIA. - <30>LYMPHOVASCULAR INVASION</30> IDENTIFIED. - <31>PERINEURAL INVASION</31> IDENTIFIED. - MARGINS NEGATIVE, 0.6 CM TO THE NEAREST INFERIOR/ANTERIOR MARGIN. - STATUS POST <32>NEOADJUVANT CHEMOTHERAPY</32>. 2. <33>DUCTAL CARCINOMA</33> ***** ***** (<34>DCIS</34>).
