2013. This scan revealed an interval decrease in the <1>mediastinal lymphadenopathy</1> since the prior exam with an enlarged <2>AP window node</2> measuring 11 mm as compared to the prior measurement of 15 mm in short axis. However there was a new <3>AP window lymph node</3> with market hypermetabolic activity. Additionally the <4>mass within the lingula of the lung</4> measured 3.4 x 2.2 cm as compared to the prior measurement of 2.9 x 2 cm. Within the abdomen and pelvis, heterogeneous uptake was noted with defects in the <5>liver</5> suggestive of <6>cysts</6>. The scan also revealed <7>diverticulosis</7> with no findings of <8>diverticulitis</8>. There was a ***** defect within the <9>right adnexa</9> likely representing an <10>ovarian cyst</10>. There was heterogeneous <11>bone marrow uptake</11> noted with no hypermetabolic activity to suggest <12>metastatic disease</12>. The patient now presents to <13>UCSF</13> for ongoing treatment recommendations and would like to proceed with the <14>biopsy of the lung lesion</14>. She reports having continued <15>chest pain</15>, similar to that which she experienced in July. She reports having a high pain tolerance but at times this pain is the worst she has ever experienced. She denies any <16>fevers</16> or <17>chills</17>. She has no <18>nausea</18> or <19>vomiting</19>, significant <20>cough</20> or <21>dyspnea</21> associated with the chest pain. She is accompanied today by her father who seems extremely supportive. The patient is an excellent historian and record *****, and is adamant to clarify any discrepancies and ***** in the medical record provided by *****. Past Medical History Diagnosis Date Breast <22>cancer</22> Anemia Anxiety Left ventricular dysfunction with reduced left ventricular function ***** in ***** after <23>adriamycin</23> Depression Autonomic neuropathy Symptoms developed after <24>chemotherapy</24> GERD (<25>gastroesophageal reflux disease</25>) Diverticulosis Migraine headache Peripheral neuropathy Osteopenia Palpitations Past Surgical History
``` 
